/**
 * Phase 2 EXECUTOR: one step of one DedicatedJob against the upstream API.
 *
 * Pure apart from the injected client, so every write path is unit-tested
 * against a recorded/mocked client (test/dedicated-ops.test.ts) — no real
 * upstream write is ever made by a test.
 *
 * The worker (worker/dedicated-jobs.ts) calls `runJobStep` on a claimed job;
 * a step either finishes (DONE / FAILED) or returns WAITING with its `state`,
 * and the worker calls it again ~10 s later (polling an upstream task / order).
 *
 * HARD SAFETY RULES (enforced here, before any write):
 *   - the target is ALWAYS the service name stored on OUR DedicatedServer row
 *     (customers only ever pass our server id; the action layer looks it up);
 *   - a service name that belongs to platform infrastructure (any Node's
 *     providerServerId, plus Setting dedicated_ovh_protected_services) is
 *     refused outright — a mistyped service name can never reboot a node;
 *   - IPs for rDNS / firewall must be inside the server's own IP blocks, read
 *     from upstream for that service, never from the client;
 *   - `dryRun` sends nothing: the step records what it WOULD do and finishes.
 * Out-of-band access stays Nxeon's: nothing here creates any login inside the
 * customer's OS; reinstall uses only the customer's own SSH key.
 */
